message: "If you use or reference FC_V1 in academic, educational, or engineering work, please cite this project."

title: "FC_V1: ESP32-Based Flight Computer Functional Prototype"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Roshan"
    given-names: "Rajnish"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-21"

abstract: >-
  FC_V1 is an ESP32-based experimental flight-computer prototype developed
  by Roshan Aerospace Industries. The system integrates BMP280 barometric
  sensing, MPU6050 inertial sensing, OLED diagnostics, deterministic
  flight-state logic, recovery-servo actuation, status indication, and
  post-landing recovery-beacon functionality. The completed prototype was
  subjected to repeated simulated flight-event bench testing and is
  classified as an Integrated Functional Prototype — Bench Verified.
  FC_V1 is not flight-qualified hardware.

keywords:
  - flight computer
  - ESP32
  - embedded systems
  - aerospace
  - avionics
  - BMP280
  - MPU6050
  - recovery system
  - flight-state machine
  - engineering prototype

